<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:12Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Von der Leyen in Greenland with EU investments amid Trump pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32c913073c2d547b2c152eb55f62300319a12a4450ef9e5452e7e95e116f61a3</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:56:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T03:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/von-der-leyen-in-greenland-with-eu-investments-amid-trump-pressure/a-79109197--69fffd262643.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/von-der-leyen-in-greenland-with-eu-investments-amid-trump-pressure/a-79109197?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU is preparing a major investment package and closer political ties with the Danish Arctic territory amid Donald Trump's demand for greater US control of the mineral-rich island.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Preliminary official results show AfD tops vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec0dc58863cd35ee1660e42bfbd7c3f02ea826c5949477daf7b7cc549f449539</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:56:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T01:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-preliminary-official-results-show-afd-tops-vote/live-78754934--3155eec2c7fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-preliminary-official-results-show-afd-tops-vote/live-78754934?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) party won the Saxony-Anhalt state election but failed to secure an absolute majority in the state parliament. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Several killed in Amazon cargo plane crash in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7718cfa192930b208f588794dc638a604e9dddc83f42ceeedcb5d9fff1f0e2b2</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:56:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T23:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/several-killed-in-amazon-cargo-plane-crash-in-miami/a-79107365--4869fc3bcedd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/several-killed-in-amazon-cargo-plane-crash-in-miami/a-79107365?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least five people have died after a cargo plane crashed at Miami International Airport. The aircraft overran a runway, struck several vehicles and caught fire.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys Witkoff and Kushner hold Ukraine talks after meeting Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5db568c2736ae68dace514436b500366895400fb9a6fd12ae8e775b07c3f0684</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T22:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779--687b66a14041.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner held talks with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Kyiv, seeking to revive efforts to end the war. But the latest diplomatic push seems to have produced no breakthrough.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AfD wants to form a government in Saxony-Anhalt — but how?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03b9d99258ba2fddacd590fdf638667ed2e45453ad329aac3a668707f841fecf</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T21:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-wants-to-form-a-government-in-saxony-anhalt-but-how/a-79107331--c787b4b85cbe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-wants-to-form-a-government-in-saxony-anhalt-but-how/a-79107331?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following its record-breaking success in the state election, the far-right AfD in Saxony-Anhalt is aiming to form a government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Digesting the AfD's landmark election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea3744d4b0d92916096e1092f540c14cd22a6feca65f066770781afb22f29085</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T21:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-digesting-the-afd-s-landmark-election-win/a-79103981--03f4036eaf84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-digesting-the-afd-s-landmark-election-win/a-79103981?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With well over 40% for the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD), Saxony-Anhalt has witnessed a landmark election night. DW's reporters were on the ground.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Election fraud claims spread in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66957e19fe1c2d50ced2350b8f3fc15cb4ee014521fae2d8b14a8f8a94b9e9ba</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T19:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-election-fraud-claims-spread-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79093254--984abe33c1c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-election-fraud-claims-spread-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79093254?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">False and misleading claims are raising questions about the integrity of the election in Saxony-Anhalt. DW Fact Check takes a closer look.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt's state election will have a nationwide impact</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ca133f57184e47fabf2d9254645a10d543f35e557aea07dadc77855e4e577c1</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T18:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-s-state-election-will-have-a-nationwide-impact/a-78874569--8cf3f82cd3a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-s-state-election-will-have-a-nationwide-impact/a-78874569?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The election in the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt could have dramatic consequences for Germany's federal government. Pollsters point to dissatisfaction with Chancellor Merz as one reason for his party's poor showing.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Germany's postal voting system isn't rigged</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c71468692fca48f92c1c3ba17281714a8a63112aaa7cdd6aa5723377e5202a7</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T18:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-postal-voting-system-isn-t-rigged/a-78958438--ffb06136be22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-postal-voting-system-isn-t-rigged/a-78958438?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of Germany's state elections in September, rumors began circulating on social media claiming that postal voting is not secure — claims that have also been made about other elections. Here's why they're wrong.</summary><category term="German election" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt election: Why the AfD is so strong</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7df601728548cbed4a8170283b57456f277092e9a8bacfd84f542845a0caf522</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:57:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T18:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-election-why-the-afd-is-so-strong/a-78482588--f7f12ed5af71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-election-why-the-afd-is-so-strong/a-78482588?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD has emerged as the strongest party in Germany's eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt by a wide margin. What is driving support for the far right in this predominantly rural eastern German state?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli strikes on Lebanon kill several despite truce</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cb3fe946d85a6e6bbc08514d527fc69d84bc89958fa24a0c667051e75691536</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israeli-strikes-on-lebanon-kill-several-despite-truce/a-79065011--55ceb327e7e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-strikes-on-lebanon-kill-several-despite-truce/a-79065011?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Lebanon's President Joseph Aoun has appealed to the international community to "take immediate action to stop these violations" of the ceasefire agreement between Israel and Lebanon.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Rahul Gandhi backs student protests in Maharashtra</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53c094f769e7cc466509d949fada0e570049059a57ebcbe8bee263cccf62a4fe</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-rahul-gandhi-backs-student-protests-in-maharashtra/live-79043198--c16d7d5783ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-rahul-gandhi-backs-student-protests-in-maharashtra/live-79043198?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition Rahul Gandhi has said that students are "tormented" by the ruling Bharatiya Janata Party. The Congress politician has demanded immediate action into the demands of Maharashtra student protesters. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, Kosovo unite against ticks carrying deadly virus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3af635e54db9b42fb65da55928b931a2daa42682be7e8ba020eaa86ebd796734</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223--2c267f5d11c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has high-security labs while Kosovo has Hyalomma ticks and experience with the deadly Crimean-Congo hemorrhagic fever. Working together, German and Kosovar scientists are fighting the disease and its vectors.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany plans anti-drone shield over Leipzig attack — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9411563f23efe3520750832694c85af0a2e8944277722abd2ec4a53a13b118bf</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-plans-anti-drone-shield-over-leipzig-attack-report/a-79052604--572615382eed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-plans-anti-drone-shield-over-leipzig-attack-report/a-79052604?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several German cities will receive rapidly deployable units capable of defending against drone strikes on critical infrastructure, according to Bild am Sonntag newspaper.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How climate change and food insecurity could fuel future conflicts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed1ecd43b83ba3be9d6d61611f6219f347c9161983f5185da63028d0c8f293e9</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T07:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-and-food-insecurity-could-fuel-future-conflicts/a-78871431--8e63f64c4115.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-and-food-insecurity-could-fuel-future-conflicts/a-78871431?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Climate change, conflict, and trade tensions are putting pressure on the global food system. New research suggests the biggest risk is not food shortages, but whether societies can peacefully adapt to change.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia: Flights canceled as Anak Krakatau volcano erupts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6f4fc06bd30f8dd2a496b9ed43b20032f8ac5bdcd59366521e23a6f0c7b18a2</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T07:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-flights-canceled-as-anak-krakatau-volcano-erupts/a-79050871--17392aeed85d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-flights-canceled-as-anak-krakatau-volcano-erupts/a-79050871?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The spread of ash after the volcanic eruption of Anak Krakatau has impacted thousands of passengers, as flights were canceled at Jakarta's international airport.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ebola: Why children are last to be treated in medical crises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:679ec7e61e50941d5bc4b8ce6539402e6abda01a315c5c33ba9cd84cc132d908</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T06:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ebola-why-children-are-last-to-be-treated-in-medical-crises/a-79050107--c059b44b485e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ebola-why-children-are-last-to-be-treated-in-medical-crises/a-79050107?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In the latest Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo, children are more likely to die than adults. But it's not always due to the disease. Specific medicines for younger people are often harder to come by.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary begins hunt for corrupt regime's billions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80717c624f94ae434abcfd94e8e9e0c89c1646cb50aa04bb00060d1feed3159e</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T05:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-begins-hunt-for-corrupt-regime-s-billions/a-79047176--0dd17c410606.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-begins-hunt-for-corrupt-regime-s-billions/a-79047176?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's new prime minister promised he would recover billions stolen or diverted by the previous administration. A new "super authority" is about to begin that work. Its success or failure will have a big impact.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys meet with Putin, leave Russia for Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90649e75d63eb2ade47d6fd0ac2aa193e0c774c8ba68f994b211fd36f9e61ad3</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T22:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-meet-with-putin-leave-russia-for-kyiv/a-79040773--6af20c7cc1f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-meet-with-putin-leave-russia-for-kyiv/a-79040773?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jared Kushner and Steve Witkoff met with Russian President Vladimir Putin in Moscow to try to revive talks to end the war in Ukraine. The US envoys are also scheduled to visit Kyiv on Sunday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German company successfully launches rocket to space</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9316100a48bb5db26090e6d69d25e8098754eb0b7bf364e94279e5e222d49229</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T22:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-company-successfully-launches-rocket-to-space/a-79050717--59c961471bc2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-company-successfully-launches-rocket-to-space/a-79050717?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bavaria-based Isar Aerospace managed to launch its Spectrum rocket into orbit, 18 months after its first attempt. This is the first such launch from European soil.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Croatia: Toxic waste protest draws tens of thousands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:658c46681ac9a81c7d08c3d356dcae11a6c09532240bc033f233f33cf62439b3</id><updated>2026-09-07T04:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T17:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228--9dec1bdce80c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Zagreb demonstrators demanded that the government come up with a plan to clear illegal toxic waste in 20 days. Prime Minister Plenkovic has promised to tackle the issue.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry></feed>
